{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 4, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1\nTHE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS A STATEMENT THAT HAS BEEN DEBATED BY MANY FOR CENTURIES. IT RAISES QUESTIONS ABOUT THE ROLE OF INDIVIDUALS IN SOCIETY AND THEIR RESPONSIBILITY TO UPHOLD THE LAW, EVEN IF THEY DISAGREE WITH IT. THIS SENTENCE ALSO IMPLIES THAT THERE ARE CIRCUMSTANCES UNDER WHICH DISOBEYING THE LAW IS JUSTIFIED, WHICH CAN LEAD TO A SLIPPERY SLOPE OF MORAL RELATIVISM. THE ISSUE WITH THIS STATEMENT IS THAT IT DOES NOT PROVIDE CLEAR GUIDELINES ON WHAT CONSTITUTES A \"BAD\" LAW, LEAVING IT TO INDIVIDUAL INTERPRETATION.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2\nFURTHERMORE, THE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" OVERLOOKS THE IMPORTANCE OF THE RULE OF LAW IN MAINTAINING SOCIAL ORDER. LAWS ARE ENACTED TO PROTECT THE RIGHTS AND INTERESTS OF CITIZENS, AND DISREGARDING THEM CAN HAVE SERIOUS CONSEQUENCES FOR BOTH THE INDIVIDUAL AND SOCIETY AS A WHOLE. INSTEAD OF ENCOURAGING PEOPLE TO DISOBEY LAWS THEY DISAGREE WITH, IT WOULD BE MORE PRODUCTIVE TO ENCOURAGE THEM TO WORK WITHIN THE SYSTEM TO CHANGE THE LAWS THEY BELIEVE ARE UNJUST. THIS APPROACH WOULD PROMOTE A MORE CONSTRUCTIVE AND RESPECTFUL FORM OF CIVIL DISOBEDIENCE, RATHER THAN SIMPLY DISREGARDING THE LAW.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": "AGR", "logprob": -7.521823135903105e-05}, {"token": "APH", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " ", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -6.437280717364047e-06}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.0006277974462136626}, {"token": " SENT", "logprob": -0.22611431777477264}, {"token": "ENCE", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.002806892851367593}, {"token": "IF", "logprob": -9.775113539944869e-06}, {"token": " THE", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " LAW", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " IS", "logprob": 0.0}, {"